#Single-cell mapping of regulatory DNA-protein interactions

DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.05.014

A study introducing docking and deamination followed by sequencing (D&D-seq), a single-cell method that uses a nanobody-coupled base editor to record DNA-protein interactions through targeted base editing.

Keywords: Single Cell, Gene Regulation, DNA-Protein Interactions, Base Editing, Epigenomics
